h Platform for Early Detection of Alzheimer’s and Other Dementias in Primary Care\",\"description\":\"The Linus Health platform empowers PCPs with digital, AI-based solutions to help them identify and intervene on brain disorders even before symptoms appear\",\"domain\":\"bit.ly\"},\"video_url\":null,\"belowTheFold\":false}\" class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-gap-12 pc-padding-16 pc-reset bg-primary-zk6FDl outline-detail-vcQLyr pc-borderRadius-md sizing-border-box-DggLA4 pressable-lg-kV7yq8 font-text-qe4AeH tweet-fWkQfo twitter-embed\">Linus Health@linushealthIt's a big day for #brainhealth! Purpose-built for #primarycare, our new platform empowers PCPs with next-generation assessment solutions to advance early detection and intervention efforts for #Alzheimers & other dementias. Learn more now:\n\nbit.lyLinus Health Launches First iPad-Based Brain Health Platform for Early Detection of Alzheimer’s and Other Dementias in Primary Care1:16 PM · Jul 27, 20224 Reposts · 9 LikesInstalled on an iPad, the platform offers both a cognitive assessment and patient questionnaire, then analyzes their results to assess each patient’s current cognitive abilities and future risk of developing a neurodegenerative disease.\n\nNext I’m going to talk about the progress AI is making with images and cells. (Video)\n\nIn this rotating 3D UMAP image, each point represents a single protein image, colored according to protein localization categories. Collectively it forms a highly detailed map of the full diversity of protein localizations. Credit: CZ Biohub\n\nRead on with a free trial or premium subscription. The main benefit is more content. \n\nGet 14 day free trial\n\nContinue reading this post for free, courtesy of Michael Spencer.\n\nClaim my free postOr purchase a paid subscription.PreviousNext© 2026 Michael Spencer · Privacy ∙ Terms ∙ Collection notice Start your SubstackGet the appSubstack is the home for great culture\n        \n\n        \n            \n